To save your spreadsheet as a .csv file

1.Open your file in your spreadsheet program.

2.Click on File and choose Save As.

3.Under Save as type, choose CSV (Comma delimited). 

4.Click Save. You may see a message that your file "may contain features that are not compatible with CSV." This message is to inform you that any formatting you may have (such as colors or bold text) and any formulas will not be preserved in the CSV formatted file. Click Yes to continue.

 

To import the file into PHDWin

1.Go to the Home Ribbon (Tools Section), click on Add/Import and select Import.

2.Choose the file to import using one:

oFrom My Computer - to browse for your *.csv file. 

3.Choose the Scenario you'd like to import the data to. 

·The scenario that you choose acts as a filter, and only cases in that scenario will be updated. 

·If you are importing qualified data, the primary qualifier for that scenario will be updated. Qualified data include expenses, investments, multipliers, ownership, prices, projections & shrinkage. 

·If you are adding new cases, they will also be added to the scenario you choose.

4.Choose to Display Log file Always, Never or On Error. 

5.If no matching ID code is found between your import file and PHDWin, you can choose to Add Unmatched Cases or Skip Unmatched Cases.

6.Click on Map Data to open the Import Center - Mapping. This is where you will map up the fields in your spreadsheet to the correct inputs in PHDWin.

7.If this is the first time you have done this type of import, you will need to click on the Plus button next to Layout to add a new one. If you plan to do the same type of import multiple times, you can see the section on Reusing import layouts.

 

